<!-- Frequently asked questions page content -->
<section>
  <h1>Frequently Asked Questions</h1>
  <p>Find helpful information before your visit to AquaVerse.</p>

  <!-- Opening times question and answer -->
  <h2>What are AquaVerse opening times?</h2>
  <p>AquaVerse is open every day from 9am to 6pm.</p>

  <!-- Accessibility question and answer -->
  <h2>Is AquaVerse wheelchair accessible?</h2>
  <p>Yes. AquaVerse has step-free access, lifts and accessible toilets throughout the aquarium.</p>

  <!-- Family facilities question and answer -->
  <h2>Are there facilities for families with young children?</h2>
  <p>Yes. Baby-changing facilities are available, and pushchairs can be used throughout most areas of the aquarium.</p>

  <!-- Food question and answer -->
  <h2>Can I bring food and drinks?</h2>
  <p>Visitors may bring a packed lunch and enjoy it in the designated picnic area.</p>

  <!-- Visit length question and answer -->
  <h2>How long should I allow for my visit?</h2>
  <p>Most visitors spend around two to three hours exploring the aquarium and its experiences.</p>

  <!-- Photography question and answer -->
  <h2>Can I take photographs?</h2>
  <p>Yes. Photography is welcome, but please do not use flash near the animal exhibits.</p>
</section>

